    "devalue": "BLOCKER: force ^5.8.1 to include GHSA-77vg-94rm-hx3p (DoS via sparse array deserialization) fix; astro 5.x pulls 5.6.x by default which is in the affected range >=5.6.3, <=5.8.0",
    "hono": "BLOCKER: force >=4.12.25 to carry the >=4.12.18 fixes plus serve-static path traversal (GHSA-wwfh-h76j-fc44), CORS wildcard reflection (GHSA-88fw-hqm2-52qc), Set-Cookie merge (GHSA-j6c9-x7qj-28xf), body-limit bypass (GHSA-rv63-4mwf-qqc2), and Lambda@Edge header drop (GHSA-wgpf-jwqj-8h8p); @modelcontextprotocol/sdk transitively pulls older hono",
    "@hono/node-server": "BLOCKER: force >=1.19.13 to pair with hono >=4.12.25 override; pre-1.19 cannot start against hono 4.12.x",
    "vite": "BLOCKER: bound >=6.4.2 <8 to capture dev-server path-traversal + fs.deny fixes while staying compatible with vitest/@vitest 3.x and the astro stack; vite 8 release is a breaking major we have not planned for",
    "postcss": "BLOCKER: force >=8.5.18 to include GHSA-qx2v-qp2m-jg93 XSS-via-unescaped-style-tag and GHSA-r28c-9q8g-f849 sourceMappingURL path-traversal (arbitrary .map file disclosure, patched 8.5.18) fixes; vite/marpit transitives otherwise hold tree at 8.5.8",
    "fast-uri": "BLOCKER: force >=3.1.3 to include GHSA-q3j6-qgpj-74h6 (encoded path-separator normalization), GHSA-v39h-62p7-jpjc (encoded authority delimiter), and GHSA-4c8g-83qw-93j6 (host confusion via failed IDN canonicalization; vulnerable >=3.0.0 <3.1.3) fixes; transitive consumers (fastify-swagger, ajv-formats) otherwise hold older versions. Bounded <4 because the only consumer in this tree is ajv@8.20.0, which declares fast-uri ^3.0.1; an unbounded range would drag the untested 4.x major into the MCP SDK's schema validator.",
    "fast-xml-builder": "BLOCKER: force >=1.1.7 to include GHSA-5wm8-gmm8-39j9 attribute-quote injection fix; aws-sdk @aws-sdk/xml-builder transitively pulls older fast-xml-parser/fast-xml-builder",
    "ip-address": "BLOCKER: force ^10.1.1 to include GHSA-v2v4-37r5-5v8g (XSS in Address6 HTML-emitting methods) fix; express-rate-limit@8.3.1 pulls 10.1.0 which is in the affected <= 10.1.0 range",
    "protobufjs": "BLOCKER: force >=7.5.6 to clear the 7.x advisories (GHSA-66ff/2pr8/fx83/75px/jvwf/685m/q6x5/xq3m all affected <= 7.5.5) — npm picks 8.2.0+ for the otlp-transformer chain which also clears the 8.0.0-8.0.1 critical RCE; @opentelemetry/sdk-node is pinned in .syncpackrc.json so we cannot bump the outer tree",
    "@grpc/proto-loader": "BLOCKER: nested override pins protobufjs ^7.5.6 inside the @grpc/proto-loader chain since proto-loader@0.8.x requires the 7.x major and cannot accept 8.x; pairs with the outer protobufjs >=7.5.6 override which handles the 8.x consumers",
    "zod": "BLOCKER: force ^4.4.3 across the whole tree so @modelcontextprotocol/sdk and the cli workspace share the same physical zod copy; without the override the SDK satisfies its 'zod: ^3.25 || ^4.0' range with the older zod@3.25.x that other transitives drag in, creating two zod installs whose v4/core $ZodType interfaces TS treats as distinct nominal types (build breaks at registerTool inputSchema)",
    "astro": "BLOCKER: astro's config validator (validateConfigRefined) was written against zod v3 and calls config.image.remotePatterns.length on the parsed shape; under the root zod ^4.4.3 override it gets undefined and the build crashes with 'Cannot read properties of undefined (reading length)'. Nest a zod ^3.25.76 override scoped to astro to match astro's own peer dep declaration. @astrojs/sitemap and @astrojs/rss already declare zod ^4 themselves so they stay on the root override.",
    "js-yaml": "BLOCKER: force >=4.2.0 <5.0.0 to include GHSA-h67p-54hq-rp68 (quadratic-complexity DoS via repeated merge-key aliases) fix while staying off the v5 major; @astrojs/markdown-remark and astro transitively pull js-yaml@4.1.1, and @astrojs/markdown-remark's `import yaml from \"js-yaml\"` default import breaks under js-yaml 5.x's ESM-only export shape (observed as a hard `astro build` SyntaxError)",
    "gray-matter": "BLOCKER: nested override pins js-yaml ^3.15.0 inside the gray-matter chain since gray-matter's frontmatter parser is written against the js-yaml v3 API and cannot accept v4; GHSA-h67p-54hq-rp68 covers two disjoint ranges (>=4.0.0 <=4.1.1 AND <3.15.0), so the v3 line also needed bumping to its final 3.15.0 patch release",
    "linkify-it": "BLOCKER: force >=5.0.1 to include GHSA-22p9-wv53-3rq4 (quadratic-complexity DoS in LinkifyIt#match) fix; markdown-it (via @marp-team/marpit) transitively pulls linkify-it@5.0.0",
    "brace-expansion@^1.1.7": "BLOCKER: clear GHSA-3jxr-9vmj-r5cp (DoS via exponential-time expansion of consecutive non-expanding {} groups; vulnerable <1.1.16 || >=3.0.0 <5.0.7) for the six eslint/minimatch@3 edges that request ^1.1.7. Pin to 1.1.18 (the patched 1.x, raised from 1.1.16 for GHSA-rgw5-rvv9-x895: the CVE-2026-14257 maxLength mitigation was incomplete, intermediate arrays stayed unbounded) rather than blanket-bumping to v5: brace-expansion v5 became ESM-only and its CommonJS build changed from `module.exports = expand` to a NAMED export `{ expand, EXPANSION_MAX }`, so minimatch@3's `var expand = require('brace-expansion'); expand(pattern)` throws 'expand is not a function' and eslint crashes. 1.1.16 keeps the callable default export and is out of the vulnerable range.",
    "brace-expansion@^5.0.5": "BLOCKER: clear GHSA-3jxr-9vmj-r5cp and GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg (unbounded expansion LENGTH — expand() caps the result count but not each result's size, so chained brace groups OOM the process; vulnerable <=5.0.7, patched 5.0.8) plus GHSA-rgw5-rvv9-x895 (the 5.0.8 maxLength mitigation was incomplete, intermediate arrays stayed unbounded; completed in 5.0.9) for the single top-level minimatch@10 edge that requests ^5.0.5. This consumer expects the v5 named-export API, so it stays on the v5 line — kept separate from the ^1.1.7 override above so neither consumer is forced across brace-expansion's v4->v5 export-shape break.",
    "qs": "BLOCKER: force >=6.16.0 to clear GHSA-x5fp-wj9c-mxmx (arrayLimit/throwOnLimitExceeded bypass via bracket-key comma parsing, affected >=6.14.2 <=6.15.3) and GHSA-4mjr-xmp4-gh2g (stringify DoS via a non-callable constructor.isBuffer, affected >=2.2.5 <6.16.0), both fixed in 6.16.0. Both reach PRODUCTION deps, where the audit gate has zero tolerance: express declares qs ^6.14.0 and body-parser declares qs ^6.15.2, and npm resolved 6.15.2 for both, so neither range moves on its own. Bounded <7 because no 7.x exists and an unbounded range would adopt an untested major into express's query parser."
